WEBVTT

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:04.700
Total Eclipse is finally 
heading for its climax.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.960
In this episode, we'll 
review the story so far

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.320
and show you some things that will allow 
you to enjoy that climax 10 times as much!

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.620
I want to return what I 
was given, what I took.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.800
Don't worry even if you've 
never seen the show before.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.650
If you watch this you can still follow it.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.290
You can fall in love with me.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:32.380
And we'll also be introducing the new 
opening and ending that start next week!

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.430
Pre-Climax Special, blast off!

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.900
<b>Finally, the Climax! 
Now you can enjoy it ten times as much!</b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.900
<b>Setting</b>

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:17.740
<b>Soviet Territory</b>

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:17.740
<b>Yukon River            Yukon Base</b>

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:17.740
<b>American Territory</b>

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.850
The story is set in the Yukon base, which lies 
at the border of Soviet and American territory.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.830
Wow!

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.960
A Jain-10 from the Unified Front of China,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.120
and an EU Tornado!

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:34.020
The next-generation TSF technology 
development project, AKA Project Prominence.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.660
The UN provides this area for countries 
who lost their territory to the BETA

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.660
as a place to develop their TSFs.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:53.190
<b>Yukon Base</b>

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:47.140
Its most important goal is to 
speed the development of TSFs

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.640
through information and technology 
sharing in a location

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:53.610
where test pilots and prototypes 
gather from all over the world.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.460
It's been almost 20 years since 
the BETA invasion of Earth began,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.070
and humanity has lost most of Eurasia 
to them as the war enters a stalemate.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.260
The Soviet Union borrows back 
the territory of Alaska,

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.660
which it once sold to the US, and 
transfers its government there.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:18.170
The Yukon base, which America had been 
building at the time, is given to the UN.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.640
Let's go!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:28.410
The next-generation TSF 
technology development project,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:31.270
AKA Project Prominence is presently underway.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.740
Yuuya and the Argos Test Flight are 
participating in the XFJ project,

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.360
a sub-project of Prominence.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.610
<b>Argos Test Flight</b>

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.620
A Turkish captain.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:47.740
Italy.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.500
Sweden.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.870
Nepal.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:58.340
The members of Argos Flight are all top 
Eishi from their respective countries.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.640
There's a reason they've been 
sent here to the rear lines.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.050
I figured Chobi'd be coming.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.770
Test pilots are tasked with pushing 
their prototypes to their limits,

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.920
and so only the best Eishi can become one.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:22.240
Oh, I missed?

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.160
They never smiled.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:30.120
They'd fought on the front lines, and 
being sent to the rear lines upset them.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.290
You need to enjoy yourself when you can.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.500
Like that.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.650
Enjoying the peace that their comrades 
on the front lines couldn't,

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:43.050
and sending them the new 
TSFs they're developing.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:51.010
The test pilots know that they're acting 
as an investment in the future of humanity.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.690
That's something they shared with 
everyone else who came before them.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.730
...repaying those who came before them.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:02.440
They're giving me what they were given.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.150
<b>Meeting</b>

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:07.860
I can't believe that.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:09.030
It's true.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:14.580
The Argos Flight was formed as part 
of the joint Japan-US XFJ project.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:17.410
Two of its members are...

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.780
You're inexperienced.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.130
<b>XFJ Project Japanese Project Leader
Japanese Royal Guard
Lt. Yui Takamura</b>

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.500
Lt. Yui Takamura heads the 
Japanese side of the project.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.740
And...

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.140
Come on, Lieutenant!

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.510
I'll fight you!

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:38.270
<b>XFJ Project Test Pilot
American Army
Ensign Yuuya Bridges</b>

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.580
And Ensign Yuuya Bridges, a half-Japanese 
American from the American Army.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.200
Yui is from an old and proper family who 
are personal servants of the Emperor.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:50.990
You're too high!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.080
Ruled by her past experiences 
and her position,

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:01.530
she's lived her whole life motivated by 
a desire to help others, to save Japan.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.750
Anti-laser smoke!

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.770
Yuuya, however...

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:13.390
That's why I told you not to trust Japs!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.500
No, father!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.440
Because of his race and birth, both he and 
his mother suffered severe discrimination.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.040
He believes becoming a Top Eishi

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.920
is the only way to get others 
to accept him and his mother,

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.300
and this desire to help himself 
has been his only motivation.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.840
You had them protect you. 
You had them cover for you.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.810
That little game where you were 
all friends in the same Flight.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:47.520
Their different values stop 
them from accepting each other,

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.490
and the two clash repeatedly.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:53.050
<b>Growth</b>

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.720
Yuuya's only interest had 
been in improving himself,

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:03.300
but as he meets and interacts with the rest 
of Yukon base, he begans to change his mind.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.650
The railgun you worked on saved everyone.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.660
I guess the Japanese aren't that bad.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.380
When Argos visited Kamchatka 
to test their TSFs,

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.570
Yuuya met someone who would change his life.

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:22.620
...and I'm so close to the front lines.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.800
Looks like you're taking it easy.

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:27.130
Is that how a hero gets to act?

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:34.970
Fikatsia Latrova, head of the 
USSR's ace Zhar Battalion.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.180
<b>Soviet Army
Zhar Battalion Commander
Commander Fikatsia Latrova</b>

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:41.040
But that immaturity of yours is clouding 
your eyes from the bigger picture.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:42.940
The bigger picture?

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.850
What are you fighting against?

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.490
When you blame something outside yourself 
for your own failure to do something,

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.930
the only thing you can 
convince is your own heart.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.410
You can never convince anyone else.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.240
What are you talking about?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.690
If you can't take it all, decide 
what you're going to abandon.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.250
That's what your fight is, kid.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.100
At first, Yuuya couldn't 
understand what her words meant.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.720
Tatiana!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.600
So in the end we're just 
pawns to be sacrificed?

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.580
Watch over me, everyone.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.890
I'll take revenge for you.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:30.640
But when Latrova sacrifices herself 
and shows him how an Eishi lives,

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.050
he learns the meaning 
and weight of her words.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:41.200
The Zhar Battalion was wiped out?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.600
I was pretending not to see how so 
many other people were protecting me.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:47.670
But watch me now.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.080
I swear to all of you.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:57.220
Someday, I'll fight to protect 
someone, like you did.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.200
Yuuya begins to grow greatly 
as a person and an Eishi

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.290
after Latrova's words and 
his experiences at Yukon,

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:09.040
begins to accept the 
Japanese blood within him,

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.190
something he's never done before.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.190
I'm Japanese-American.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:21.240
And he sees himself reflected in the 
Japanese-American Shiranui Type 2.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.950
It's amazing. A beautiful machine.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:28.060
He finds a new goal for 
himself: seeing it completed.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.720
When he finds a place for himself in Argos, 
his obsession with avenging his past ends,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:46.230
and he swears that he'll pass on what 
his comrades gave him to someone else.

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.320
I want to return what I was given...

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.560
what I took.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.200
<b>Change</b>

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.290
I refuse to allow any Eishi 
to die in a TSF I tested.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.400
Even you Japanese.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.690
At first she clashes with him, but 
as she learns more about Yuuya,

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:17.040
Yui's heart begins to change as well.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.890
He never gave up, no matter 
how hard things got.

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:29.320
Yuuya Bridges.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.980
Why am I remembering him at a time like this?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.060
Yuuya...

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.030
What...?

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:51.720
As she sees Yuuya overcome even 
the most difficult situations

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:55.100
without ever thinking of 
his position or his family,

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:57.130
she finds himself gradually drawn to him.

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:00.170
Bridges, you...

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:03.360
You can call me Yuuya.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.930
W-What are you talking about all of a sudden?

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:12.150
What? You were just calling me that.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.320
H-H-How did you...

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:18.320
<b>Rival</b>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.570
Can I have another?

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.860
There's still plenty left.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:30.820
As she begins to get closer 
to Yuuya, new rivals appear.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.130
Yuuya Bridges.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.380
You can fall in love with me if you want.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:45.510
<b>Chinese United Front
Bao Feng Test Flight
Lt. Cui Yifei</b>

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:45.210
Lt. Cui Yifei, of the Chinese Unified
 Front's Bao Feng Test Flight.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.390
She goes after Yuuya hard, with 
the same strong personality

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.520
that's reflected in her TSF piloting.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.090
What are you doing?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:58.110
Your face is red.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.360
Is that you, Yuuya?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.100
Yuuya's former lover,

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:10.700
<b>American Army
65th Combat Training Group "Infinities"
Sharon Imes</b>

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:10.400
Sharon Imes of the 65th Combat Training 
Battalion "Infinities" appears as well.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:15.460
And the USSR Army's aces, the Scarlet Twins.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.980
You and I won't, either.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:18.920
Really?

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:24.880
<b>Soviet Army Idar Test Flight
Ensign Inia Sestina</b>

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:24.880
<b>Soviet Army Idar Test Flight
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa</b>

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.530
Ensign Inia Sestina and 
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:32.480
For some reason, Inia is very open 
with Yuuya from the very beginning,

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:32.780
That's...

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:34.050
You again?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.150
This voice, it can't be...

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:39.440
but Cryska was cold and antagonistic.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.220
Never hang out with a man like that again.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:43.940
Yes.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:47.820
We two are the only family we have.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:57.740
As Inia becomes more involved with Yuuya, 
Cryska gradually starts to change.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.630
I'd like you to tell me about Yuuya Bridges.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.590
I'm interested in him.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.400
Yuuya Bridges.

00:13:13.280 --> 00:13:14.350
Cryska?

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.000
Are you looking for Inia?

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:17.880
How did you know?

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:20.730
Can you read my mind?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.280
Think about it.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:26.200
You never talk to me unless it's about Inia.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:27.810
That's all.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.620
Oh, that wasn't much fun at all.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.650
Don't try to make it fun.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:40.130
You didn't answer right 
away, so it made me wonder.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.500
Cryska smiled?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:47.620
Cryska sees Inia approaching Yuuya,

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.720
when she's never taken an 
interest in anyone else before.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.100
No!

00:13:56.100 --> 00:14:01.490
Cryska realizes that Inia is 
causing her own feelings to change.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:03.570
Inia...

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:06.610
Do you want to be friends with Yuuya too?

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.950
Cryska has lived her whole life as a weapon,

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.300
is uncertain about how to handle these 
changes in her heart, and suffers.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:15.300
Something's strange.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.620
Whenever I think about you,

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.290
I can't concentrate.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.770
Unsure of what her feelings are,

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:30.680
she finds herself drawn to Yuuya 
as if Inia is pulling her along.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:35.890
I just want you to tell me.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:40.480
I don't know what to do from now on...

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:41.860
Darling!

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.320
Lt. Cui?

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:49.700
What will be their fate as 
these women struggle for Yuuya?

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.440
And what about Yuuya's heart?

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:57.500
Look forward to seeing what happens!

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.500
What am I doing?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:08.000
After this, Minami Kurabayashi sings 
the new opening, "Doubt the World!"

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.380
Don't miss this powerful number 
that's perfect for the climax!

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:18.680
Now we'll show you the new opening, with 
Minami Kurabayashi's "Doubt The World!"

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:24.940
<b>New Opening from Next Episode:
Minami Kuribayashi's Doubt The World.</b>

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:54.120
Now we'll show you two major points that will help 
you get ten times as much enjoyment out of the climax!

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:59.920
Deploy and continue the trial using group D.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:07.710
<b>Soviet Military Idar Test Flight Commander
Lt. Jerzy Sandek</b>

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:06.760
Lt. Jerzy Sandek, head of the 
Soviets' Idar Test Flight.

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:11.420
What exactly do you intend 
to do, Comrade Rogofsky?

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:12.810
What?

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:17.760
You've lost a front-line 
base, attacked your own side,

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.140
and then wiped out our 
all-important bomber forces...

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:28.080
In Kamchatka, he took advantage of 
the failure of his superior officer,

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:31.130
Rogofsky, to take control 
of the secret project.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:35.410
A man who's always working in the shadows 
and who will do anything for his goals.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.070
This exercise is more than just a 
test of our respective capabilities.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:44.080
It is a demonstration of 
my Polnoe Zatmeniya plan.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:51.850
At the center of Sandek's Polnoe 
Zatmeniya plan are Cryska and Inia.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:55.460
Roger.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.090
Test flights, begin your mission.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:10.560
The two of them met in a lab for the UN's 
Alternative-3 project, a secret anti-BETA project.

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:15.160
And several years later 
were conscripted by Sandek.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:19.740
Sandek's plan was taking 
place, even back then.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.280
That score is incredible...

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.860
The Terminator shows terrifying 
combat capability.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.500
This must be what happiness feels like.

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:42.400
A mysterious phenomenon called Prafka 
gives them unmatched abilities.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:50.690
Perhaps as a result, Cryska has memory 
problems and is emotionally unstable.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.440
Are you planning something?

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:57.980
Does she not remember?

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.690
You were crying, weren't you Yuuya?

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.780
You were crying?

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:05.200
What are you talking about?

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:09.960
Inia almost seems like she can read minds.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.540
...all important memories that 
made you who you are today.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.280
I thought so.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:20.260
It was worth letting him go after 
he infiltrated this facility.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.940
Cryska and Inia are caught 
up in Sandek's plot.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:25.640
Bridges.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:30.450
What will their hidden powers 
bring to Yuuya, and the world?

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.890
I'll need to get another stage for him ready.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:39.970
Two major points that will help you get ten 
times as much enjoyment out of the climax!

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.740
The battle for survival against the BETA

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:48.850
has destroyed the rules of equality, 
human rights, and freedom,

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:52.530
widening the gap between 
the haves and have-nots.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.160
J-Jacob!

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:03.130
Some are forced into a horrific war 
of attrition on the front lines.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.370
Stop it!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.140
Can't you see the friendly markers?

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:13.730
Others command the battle from 
the safety of the rear lines.

00:20:15.410 --> 00:20:18.010
We'll need to bring in more replacements.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.320
Refugees swarm from the areas 
in Eurasia under BETA control,

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:28.200
while the countries behind the battle 
lines enjoy a wartime economic boom.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.410
The tension brought by the BETA invasion

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.600
rips apart the bonds that unite humanity.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:41.220
I am a test pilot with the 331st Special Experimental 
Development Squad of the Soviet Central Strategic Research Corps.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:42.710
Ensign Cryska Barchenowa.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:46.890
Right, right. An elite from the capital.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:47.970
Shut up!

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:54.220
Most of the staff at Yukon base are from refugee 
camps from nations which lost their land to the BETA.

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:56.170
We're both soldiers in the Soviet-

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:57.160
No.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:58.520
You're a Russian.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.890
What the hell is a "Soviet" anyway?

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.650
It's not even the name of a country.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.860
We're the ones dying out here,

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:10.450
while you guys are slacking 
off on the rear lines!

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.600
And this is from me.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:20.000
I don't think there's anybody out there 
who doesn't have their own problems.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:23.010
Everybody's doing their 
best to live right now.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:30.700
Behind their smiles lie a sad 
past they never speak of.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.310
I barely remember a thing about France.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.640
The past is the past.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.900
What's most important is 
that we're alive right now.

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:45.280
The number of refugees grow 
all over the world every day.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.420
The unbridgeable gap between 
the rich and poor,

00:21:48.420 --> 00:21:50.170
where the burden falls 
entirely on the have-nots,

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:53.080
will cast a giant shadow on the world.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:59.810
The unfairness and dissatisfaction 
that it brings...

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:09.400
The day they reach their limit is near.

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:17.130
Did you enjoy the Total Eclipse 
Pre-Climax Special?

00:22:17.450 --> 00:22:21.040
What fate will Yuuya and his 
friends win for themselves?

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:24.040
Witness a new dawn!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:28.840
We'll end the show with 
ayami's "Revise the World."

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:31.760
The lyrics are filled with keywords 
that foreshadow future developments.

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.530
Watch both the opening and ending carefully!

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:52.050
The burning star falls through the sky

00:22:53.570 --> 00:22:58.570
From far to near

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:06.820
There's no way I could feel the heat

00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:14.120
but the cage around me seems to melt.

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:28.130
Burn it all, and show me a 
new place in the broken world

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:35.860
When two hearts are fated to overlap

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:42.290
you look at me with gentle eyes.

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:49.100
The light of judgment in 
a heart I want to protect

00:23:49.100 --> 00:24:00.120
Will its smile disappear?

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:11.800
You said before you can understand the 
peace here but you can't accept it, right?

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:14.780
Impressive. His plan was perfect.

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:19.120
Do you really believe we can 
change the world like this?

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>The World Bares its Fangs</b>

00:24:20.100 --> 00:24:22.090
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.560 --> 00:24:23.930
The World Bares its Fangs
